    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The first state to unite the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/irrawaddy-river">Irrawaddy</a> valley, ruled from Pagan, a walled city on the middle Irrawaddy dated by tradition to 849.</li><li>Its kings and subjects built some 10,000 Buddhist monuments on the plain of Bagan, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theravada-buddhism">Theravada Buddhism</a> became the faith of the realm.</li><li>Tax-free gifts of land to monasteries weakened the crown, and Mongol invasions in the 1280s broke the kingdom apart.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Myazedi inscription of 1113 repeats the same text in Pali, Mon, Pyu and Old Burmese, and it became the key to deciphering the lost Pyu language.</p></aside>
    </section>

